&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and maintain the roadmap for internal and external business processes supporting B2B go-to-market, including partners, channels, and internal teams, with a strong focus on execution and measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and continuously refine end-to-end user journeys for partners, sales, and customer-facing teams, from deal creation through onboarding and post-sale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery and requirement definition for partner, channel, and sales workflows, including pricing, quoting, onboarding, and post-sale processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs and user journeys into clear epics and user stories, and work day-to-day with engineering teams responsible for the company’s business platforms and CRM-related systems to deliver high-quality, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make practical prioritization decisions based on business impact, delivery effort, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in product management or a closely related role (Revenue Operations, Sales Operations, or Customer Success), with proven ownership of product delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of B2B business models and how partners and channels operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience supporting sales workflows, including pricing, quoting, deal lifecycle, and post-sale processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define user journeys, build and manage a product roadmap, and execute it in close collaboration with engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineers and understanding technical tradeoffs, particularly when building on top of business platforms or CRM systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product instincts, high attention to detail, and a good eye for UI/UX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with marketing or customer success processes is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with networking, security, or SASE is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

